# ============================================================================
# demo/.env.example — TEMPLATE ONLY. Copy and fill it; never commit real values.
#
# This repository commits no secrets. The running private configuration
# (`demo/.local/stack.env`) is auto-generated by `demo/setup.py` and is
# git-ignored — do not hand-edit it. This file only documents the exact format
# each credential must use. All values below are placeholders.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. OPENCODE_API_KEY — inference relay (needed for paid inference only)
#
# This key is read from an EXTERNAL dotenv that already exists on the host.
# Point setup.py at it; only this single key is copied, nothing else:
#
#     python3 demo/setup.py --opencode-env /absolute/path/to/AEion/.env
#
# Format inside that external file (one line; an `export ` prefix is also
# accepted). The value must be a simple token of letters, digits, ".", "_"
# and "-" only — no spaces, braces, quotes or other characters.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPENCODE_API_KEY=replace_with_a_simple_token_abc123

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. GitHub credential — host publisher (PLANNED; loader is NOT implemented yet)
#
# There is no variable name or file wired up today, so adding a line here does
# not enable the publisher. When it is implemented, `demo/forum/ECOSYSTEM.md`
# ("Merge policy and GitHub credentials") requires one of:
#   - a GitHub App installed on this repository only (preferred), or
#   - a restricted fine-grained PAT: Contents write, Pull requests write,
#     Issues write, and Actions read only if check readback needs it
#     (Metadata read is implicit). Never Administration, Workflows, Secrets or
#     Environments.
# The value must go through protected host credential storage and is NEVER
# committed, echoed, written into a brief, or pasted into chat.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GITHUB_APP_* = <reserved — do not define until the publisher loader exists>
